Significance testing, particularly the paired-permutation test, has been essential for ensuring that performance differences between NLP systems are statistically significant rather than due to chance. However, practitioners have historically relied on Monte Carlo approximations because no suitable exact algorithm existed. This paper introduces an efficient exact algorithm for the paired-permutation test applicable to a specific family of structured test statistics. The proposed algorithm operates in $\mathcal{O}(GN (\log GN )(\log N ))$ time, where $N$ represents the dataset size and $G$ denotes the range of the test statistic. Experimental results indicate that our exact algorithm is 10 times faster than a Monte Carlo approximation using 200 samples on a standard dataset. Furthermore, the algorithm scales effectively; for instance, determining the $p$-value for a dataset with one million data points required only 20 minutes. This exact algorithm enables researchers to reassess the significance of cross-entropy and linguistic improvements achieved by various systems (including machine translation, text simplification, and summarization) on benchmark datasets such as SETS, SISSETT, and MTORD. Assesses the exact algorithm for the SISSETT dataset.
